---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/use-cases/discount-strategy";
const title = "Discount strategy for Shopify email";
const desc = "Decide which offer a customer can actually redeem before choosing the email that promotes it. This workflow owns offer eligibility, contribution limits and conflicts across capture, campaigns and automated messages.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Must every flow contain a discount?",
    "answer": "No. Match the message to the purchase barrier and compare the contribution of offers against useful non-discount content."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should two offers ever combine?",
    "answer": "Yes, when that combination is intentional, affordable and reflected in checkout terms. Rehearse the exact basket and keep support guidance for exceptions."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does redemption prove incremental sales?",
    "answer": "No. Redemption identifies offer use. Incrementality needs a credible comparison that includes customers who would have bought without the offer."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Workflow playbook</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Inventory the promises already in circulation</h2>
    <p>Build an offer register with campaign or flow, customer eligibility, qualifying products, minimum spend, currency, start and end timezone, redemption limit and owner. Include popup promises, affiliate codes, loyalty rewards and automatic offers. Record a promised but unused benefit separately from a redeemed benefit: blocking only after redemption leaves multiple conflicting promises in flight.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Choose an offer path, not a universal ladder</h2>
    <p>For each audience compare product proof, access, shipping benefit and price reduction against the purchase barrier. A delivery concern may call for a shipping explanation rather than a larger code. Define escalation using actual response and contribution evidence. Neither VIP status nor a previous full-price order proves that a customer should always be excluded from promotions.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Set the contribution floor with real costs</h2>
    <p>Start with merchandise revenue after discount, then subtract product cost, fulfillment, payment charges, shipping subsidy and expected returns. Do not subtract the same discount again from already net revenue. Compare percentage, fixed-amount and free-shipping offers on the same eligible basket; a larger order does not automatically make subsidized shipping cheaper than a percentage offer.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Resolve simultaneous offers at checkout</h2>
    <p>Write expected outcomes for popup plus welcome, cart plus sale, employee plus public code and loyalty plus free shipping. Decide which combinations are intended and what the shopper should see when another benefit cannot apply. Rehearse those exact baskets in the store checkout rather than infer behavior from email copy. Keep an approved exception when honoring an earlier promise is the right customer outcome.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Maintain code state through the send queue</h2>
    <p>Track issuance, dispatch, expiry and redemption separately, with the relevant customer and offer identifiers. Define whether retries reuse the code and what happens when code creation fails. A personalized greeting does not prove a code is restricted to that customer. Confirm actual restrictions and expiry in a demonstration before relying on them; remove countdown copy if the expiry cannot be enforced.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Adapt terms for market and merchandise</h2>
    <p>Translate eligibility as well as headline value. Check local currency, shipping zone, excluded collections, subscriptions, gift cards and bundles in representative baskets. Put material conditions next to the offer and repeat them on the landing page. If a market cannot redeem an offer, route to appropriate content instead of an otherwise identical email with an unusable code.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Coordinate campaigns with active automations</h2>
    <p>Use an explicit priority record for the specific offer and item, not an arbitrary customer-wide waiting period. A sale may replace a weaker cart incentive while leaving useful product help active. Update pending messages as well as future entries when terms change. Support needs the previous terms and send timestamp to answer disputes after a campaign has ended.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Measure full-price share without inventing sensitivity</h2>
    <p>Define full-price orders consistently, including shipping rewards and loyalty treatment, then segment comparable products and customer cohorts. Rising full-price share can reflect product mix rather than policy improvement. Where feasible, compare randomly assigned eligible groups receiving different offers and include all assigned customers in the outcome; coupon redemption alone excludes people who would have purchased anyway.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Rehearse failure and restore the promise</h2>
    <p>Proposed exercise, not an observed result: issue a welcome offer, schedule a cart reminder, start a competing sale, then cancel an order and retry dispatch. Check the resulting code, copy and checkout totals. Give support a documented way to honor valid earlier terms. Pause the faulty offer path and restore its prior version if eligibility or checkout behavior differs from the approved register.</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl">
    <h2>Choose tools and review the cost of operation</h2>
    <p>Ask a supplier to show issuance failure, checkout restrictions, queued-message cancellation and a cross-channel conflict using your fixtures. Count code administration, support handling and offer-report exports alongside subscription charges. Review the register when merchandising changes and investigate unexpected redemptions or margin changes; do not migrate merely because a predetermined trial length or revenue multiple has elapsed.</p>
  </div></section>
  <nav class="container pb-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4" aria-label="Related workflows"><a class="link" href="/use-cases/analytics">Measurement</a><a class="link" href="/use-cases/black-friday">Sale coordination</a><a class="link" href="/use-cases/email-design">Offer presentation</a></nav>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
